            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "しゅうしょくする (shūshoku suru) is Sino-Japanese (kango) shūshoku with the native verb suru, \"to do\": two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are shū, \"settle\" (Middle Chinese dzjuwH) and shoku, \"employment\" (tsyik) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription)."
